 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Small Path Lengths ($s \to 0$)**: As $s \to 0$, the normalization factor $N$ diverges exponentially. The term $-C$ in the exponent is explicitly included to cancel this divergence for numerical stability [S1].
-*   **Short Path Limit ($ps \ll 1$)**: The propagator approaches an unscattered delta distribution. The term $-D \hat{\omega} \cdot \hat{\omega}'$ might appear to force directions apart, but it is counteracted by the displacement weight forcing $\vec{R}/s$ to align with $(\hat{\omega} + \hat{\omega}')/2$ [S1].
+*   **Small Path Lengths ($s \to 0$)**: As $s \to 0$, the normalization factor $N$ diverges exponentially [S1]. The term $-C$ in the exponent is explicitly included to cancel this divergence for numerical stability [S1].
+*   **Short Path Limit ($ps \ll 1$)**: The propagator approaches an unscattered delta distribution [S1]. The term $-D \hat{\omega} \cdot \hat{\omega}'$ might appear to force directions apart, but it is counteracted by the displacement weight forcing $\vec{R}/s$ to align with $(\hat{\omega} + \hat{\omega}')/2$ [S1].
